{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "94805387e04969a2d76b540582bbb3166bfe423879cc9f24af0f2eae3c16a195",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-94805387e049-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Act includes two base penalties that depend on drug quantity: a 5\u2011year mandatory minimum (triggered by 5\u202fg of crack or 500\u202fg of powder) and a 10\u2011year mandatory minimum (triggered by 50\u202fg of crack or 5\u202fkg of powder)."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justices",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5a454a7240b1e92b0b9c192aeda39608cd4d257c92d7d01dfc46867ae8e19239",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5a454a7240b1-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "5a454a7240b1e92b0b9c192aeda39608cd4d257c92d7d01dfc46867ae8e19239",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5a454a7240b1-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The central legal question is whether the phrase \u201cstatutory penalties\u201d in the Fair Sentencing Act refers to sentencing ranges or to the crack\u2011quantity thresholds."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Amicus Curiae (Adam K. Mortara)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5a454a7240b1e92b0b9c192aeda39608cd4d257c92d7d01dfc46867ae8e19239",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5a454a7240b1-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Amicus Curiae (Adam K. Mortara), according to Amicus Curiae (Adam K. Mortara), amicus Mortara argues that \u201cstatutory penalties\u201d means the sentencing range, but Section\u202f2 of the Fair Sentencing Act did not modify any sentencing ranges; it only raised the crack\u2011quantity thresholds."
      }
    ],
